            <div xml:id="d417">

                <pb facs="0807" n="795" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg795"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/4–2346: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Mukden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clubb</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mukden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-04-23T17:00:00+08:00">April 23, 1946—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 24—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>47. About 40 Chinese officials most of whom were Central Govt. arrived here in 2
                    Chinese planes from Harbin on 20th, another group arrived today and it is
                    rumored more are coming. They will reputedly stay for present at Mukden.</p>
                <p>Please repeat Nanking.</p>
                <p>Movement presumably connected with Chinese belief that Harbin will go way of
                    Changchun after withdrawal Soviet troops scheduled for noon tomorrow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clubb</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
